    description: "Analogue check for WI-juzaj (Mix + npm DependencyManifest readers). Cargo.toml is read only as TOML dependency symbols for the dependency linker (toml_config.py -> linkers/dependency.py depends_on_manifest edges); it is NOT a DependencyManifest source, so Rust boundary nodes get no directness stamp (ir.create_boundary_nodes -> DependencyManifest.directness_for returns None for language 'rust'). Add a Cargo reader (workspace Cargo.toml [dependencies]/[dev-dependencies]/[build-dependencies]/[target.*.dependencies] direct, hyphen->underscore crate names; Cargo.lock [[package]] names transitive; workspace members subtracted) as a scoped 'cargo' table keyed by crate name, with a resolver mapping a boundary path's first '::' segment to a crate (std/core/alloc/crate/self/super -> none). Would also unblock WI-totob (needs the manifest's dependency names)."  # af46
    fields: {}  # af46
